{{Documentation subpage}}
{{Lua|Module:Horizontal timeline}}
'''Template:Horizontal timeline''' is used to create a horizontal timeline.
{{warning|This template is not compatible with mobile}}

==Parameters==

=== Basic plot settings ===
* {{para|border}} Border of the plot. E.g. {{code|2px solid #CFD2AA}}
* {{para|bgCol}} Background color of the plot
* {{para|width}} Width of the timeline plot. Defaults to {{code|100%}}, can be in {{code|px}} or {{code|em}} too
* {{Para|caption}} shows a centered text. Can be used to show legends. Intended to be used to label the axis
* {{Para|from}} and {{Para|to}} Necessary parameters which denotes the start and end of the timeline axis. The entire timeline (for the entire plot) including other type of rows are drawn to this scale. {{Para|to}} may or may not be greater than {{Para|from}}. (see {{Para|inc}} for more on this) If any bars described using parameters shown below lie outside these values, they will be ''trimmed'' or ''eliminated'' depending on their position.
* {{Para|inc}} Optional Increment to be added to {{Para|from}} to reach {{Para|to}} and be displayed along the axis. If not specified it will be automatically calculated. If {{Para|to}} is greater than {{Para|from}} then {{para|inc}} should be positive and vice versa. If not the outcome is undetermined.

== The row{{sub|''n''}} parameter ==

{{Para|row{{sub|''n''}}}} specifies how horizontal rows are drawn. You can have as many rows as you want. Subscript are positive integers. They specify where the row is rendered on the plot. Lower subscript indicate higher on the plot. That is {{Para|row3}} will be above {{Para|row4}}

Three differenct types of rows are possible. They are:
* {{code|scale}}: Specifies ''where'' the axis is drawn. (''how'' it is drawn can be found in the [[#Scale Row|Scale Row]] section below).
* {{code|timeline}}: Specifies where and how the bars are drawn.
* {{code|note}}: Row that contains arrow marked notes to give explanations to the graph.

===Generic parameters===
* {{Para|height}} Applies height of {{code|timeline}} and {{code|note}} rows.

Each of these types of rows have their own attributes specified with an hyphen. For example, the style of a row{{sub|''n''}} can be specified as {{Para|row{{sub|''n''}}-style}}. Full list of available attributes and their description can be found below.

=== Scale row ===

* {{Para|axis-negativeFmt}}, {{Para|axis-positiveFmt}} and {{Para|axis-zeroFmt}} Formatting options for Axis scale. If you want more customization, (like completely hiding a single label on the axis) use the following:
** {{Para|axis-''value''}} - Used to replace the value label on the axis (It will work if and only if the exact value appears on it).
** {{Para|axis-marker-''value''}} - Used to replace the marker point for a label that appears on the axis. (It will work if and only if the exact value appears on it).
* {{Para|axis-nudge}} Amount of nudge to be applied to the axis label, defaults to {{code|-1.8em}}.

|axis-marker-1878=&nbsp;
|axis-1878=&nbsp;

